# Firebase Data Rules

Read `docs/SCHEMA.md` before changing any Firestore or Storage usage.

## Collections

- `users/{uid}` — email, displayName (keep in sync with Auth profile)
- `chatRooms/{roomId}` — participants[], name?, lastMessage, updatedAt
- `chatRooms/{roomId}/messages/{messageId}` — text, senderId, createdAt

## Required patterns

```typescript
// Timestamps on write
createdAt: serverTimestamp()
updatedAt: serverTimestamp()

// User doc — always merge via syncUserDoc() in lib/users.ts
syncUserDoc(authUser, { displayName, photoURL })
```

## Home screen query (needs composite index)

`chatRooms` where `participants array-contains uid` orderBy `updatedAt` desc

Index lives in `firebase/firestore.indexes.json`.

## Security

- Rules source: `firebase/firestore.rules`, `firebase/storage.rules`
- Remind user to deploy if rules change (`yarn deploy:rules`, see `docs/SETUP.md`)
- Messages: `senderId == request.auth.uid`; whitelist `text`, `senderId`, `createdAt`; text 1–1000 chars; `createdAt` is `serverTimestamp()`
- Rooms: exactly two distinct existing UIDs on create; `participants` immutable; updates may change only `name`, `lastMessage`, `updatedAt`

## Do not

- Store passwords or secrets in Firestore
- Allow unauthenticated reads/writes in rules
- Allow a participant to set `senderId` to someone else
- Allow `participants` to grow, shrink, or be replaced after create
- Add fields without updating `docs/SCHEMA.md`
- Hardcode a Firebase project ID or API key in source
